Birgisson is an Icelandic patronymic meaning 'son of Birgir'. Notable people with the surname include:
  - Arnthor Birgisson, Swedish songwriter and producer;
  - Birgir Örn Birgisson, Icelandic basketball coach and a former professional player;
  - Gunnar Birgisson (1947–2021), Icelandic politician, a former member of the Alþingi and former mayor of Kópavogur;
  - Jón Þór Birgisson or Jónsi, the guitarist and vocalist for the Icelandic post-rock band Sigur Rós;
  - Steinar Birgisson, Icelandic former handball player who competed in the 1984 Summer Olympics.

